  "date": "2014-10",
  "title": "Invitation To Eth Day 2014",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Registration",
      "text": "Outstanding accomplishment deserve recognition. ETH Zurich will continue its tradition of awarding honorary doctorates to people whose academic achievements have been particularly remarkable on an international level. The Federal Institute of Technology will also take the opportunity to thank everyone who served our university so well this year. In addition, we will recognize selected students and faculty members of ETH Zurich for their outstanding achievements.\n\nThe president and rector of ETH Zurich cordially invite the ETH Zurich staff to attend this year's ETH Day. Join us to look back on the previous academic year and raise a glass to its many success stories.\n\nThe Ceremonial speech will be held by Martin Vetterli, President of the Swiss National Science Foundation SNSF."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Subscribe to Newsletter",
      "text": "Fanfare * * * Prof. Dr. Lino Guzzella, Rector of ETH Zurich Opening remarks * * * Musical interlude * * * Prof. Dr. Ralph Eichler, President of ETH Zurich Welcome address * * * Prof. Dr. Martin Vetterli, President of the Swiss National Science Foundation SNSF Ceremonial speech * * * Presentation of young scientists of the Department of Civil, Environmental and Geomatic Engineering * * * Musical interlude * * * Awards and prizes Remembering those we have lost Awarding of scientific and foundation prizes Awarding of the \"Golden Owl\" and the Credit Suisse Award for Best Teaching by the ETH Zurich Students Association (VSETH), with a speech by the VSETH president Awarding honorary doctorates * * * Musical conclusion Music by the Zurich Academic Orchestra"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Registration",
      "text": "We would be pleased to welcome you to this year's ETH Day. Please register online by 22 October 2014.\n\nRegister for ETH Day 2014"
    }
  ],
